 "steps": [
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Le canal",
    "en": "The channel"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "Dans un bâtiment, un poste ne se branche pas directement au switch :\n- un **cordon de brassage** court va du switch au **panneau de brassage** (dans la baie du local technique) ;\n- le **câble du mur** (lien permanent, rigide) va du dos du panneau au dos de la **prise murale** du bureau ;\n- un **cordon de poste** va de la prise au PC.\nTout cela forme le **canal** : 100 m au plus, dont 90 m de lien permanent.",
    "en": "In a building, a computer is not plugged straight into the switch:\n- a short **patch cord** goes from the switch to the **patch panel** (in the rack of the wiring closet);\n- the **in-wall cable** (permanent link, solid core) goes from the back of the panel to the back of the office **wall outlet**;\n- a **work-area cord** goes from the outlet to the PC.\nAll of this forms the **channel**: 100 m at most, of which 90 m of permanent link."
   },
   "check": {
    "type": "info"
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Brancher PC1",
    "en": "Connect PC1"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "PC1 n’est pas branché. Avec l’outil **Câble**, tirez un cordon de 3 m entre la face avant de la prise **PR1** et le port de PC1. Le lien doit monter à **1 Gb/s** jusqu’au switch, à travers la prise et le panneau.",
    "en": "PC1 is not connected. With the **Cable** tool, draw a 3 m cord between the front of outlet **PR1** and PC1’s port. The link must come up at **1 Gb/s** all the way to the switch, through the outlet and the panel."
   },
   "spot": [
    ".ntTools [data-tool=\"cable\"]",
    ".ntDev[data-id=\"pr1\"] .ntPort[data-port=\"front\"]",
    ".ntDev[data-id=\"pc1\"] .ntPort[data-port=\"eth0\"]"
   ],
   "check": {
    "type": "net-link",
    "a": "PC1",
    "b": "SW1",
    "speed": 1000
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Le canal de PC2",
    "en": "PC2’s channel"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "Choisissez les câbles du chemin de PC2 et lisez leurs longueurs dans l’inspecteur : cordon du switch au panneau, câble du mur, cordon de poste. Quelle est la longueur du canal ?",
    "en": "Select the cables on PC2’s path and read their lengths in the inspector: cord from switch to panel, in-wall cable, work-area cord. How long is the channel?"
   },
   "keep": {
    "fr": "2 + 96 + 8 = 106 m : plus que les 100 m d’un canal, et le câble du mur dépasse aussi ses 90 m.",
    "en": "2 + 96 + 8 = 106 m: more than the 100 m of a channel, and the in-wall cable also exceeds its 90 m."
   },
   "check": {
    "type": "quiz",
    "options": [
     {
      "fr": "96 m",
      "en": "96 m"
     },
     {
      "fr": "98 m",
      "en": "98 m"
     },
     {
      "fr": "106 m",
      "en": "106 m"
     },
     {
      "fr": "104 m",
      "en": "104 m"
     }
    ],
    "answer": 2
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Raccourcir le chemin",
    "en": "Shorten the path"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "L’installateur a fait un grand détour. En passant par le faux plafond, le câble du mur ne fait que **85 m** : changez sa longueur dans l’inspecteur. Prenez aussi un cordon de poste de **3 m**. L’onglet Problèmes ne doit plus signaler de canal trop long (J1203) ni de lien permanent trop long (J1204).",
    "en": "The installer took a long detour. Through the false ceiling, the in-wall cable is only **85 m**: change its length in the inspector. Also use a **3 m** work-area cord. The Problems tab must no longer report a channel that is too long (J1203) or a permanent link that is too long (J1204)."
   },
   "spot": [
    "#tab-nprop"
   ],
   "check": {
    "type": "net-ok",
    "codes": [
     "J1203",
     "J1204"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Deux postes à 1 Gb/s",
    "en": "Two computers at 1 Gb/s"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "Les deux PC ont maintenant un lien à 1 Gb/s, sans erreur.",
    "en": "Both PCs now have an error-free 1 Gb/s link."
   },
   "check": {
    "type": "net-link",
    "a": "pc",
    "b": "SW1",
    "speed": 1000
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Le ping vers la box",
    "en": "Ping the box"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "Les deux PC reçoivent leur adresse de la box. Faites un ping de chaque PC vers la box.",
    "en": "Both PCs get their address from the box. Ping the box from each PC."
   },
   "spot": [
    ".ntTools [data-tool=\"ping\"]"
   ],
   "check": {
    "type": "net-ping",
    "from": "pc",
    "to": "BOX1"
   }
  },
  {
   "title": {
    "fr": "Rigide ou souple ?",
    "en": "Solid or stranded?"
   },
   "text": {
    "fr": "Le câble du mur a des conducteurs **rigides** (monobrins), les cordons des conducteurs **souples** (multibrins). Pourquoi ?",
    "en": "The in-wall cable has **solid** conductors, the cords have **stranded** ones. Why?"
   },
   "check": {
    "type": "quiz",
    "options": [
     {
      "fr": "Le rigide transmet mieux sur une grande longueur et ne bouge plus une fois posé ; le souple supporte d’être plié et rebranché souvent",
      "en": "Solid conducts better over a long run and never moves once laid; stranded copes with being bent and replugged often"
     },
     {
      "fr": "C’est seulement une question de couleur de gaine",
      "en": "It is only a matter of jacket colour"
     },
     {
      "fr": "Le souple est réservé au PoE",
      "en": "Stranded is reserved for PoE"
     }
    ],
    "answer": 0
   }
  }
 ]
}
